---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CaptureForm from "../../components/forms/capture-form.astro";
const seo = { page_description: "Calculate PDF image resolution (DPI) and physical dimensions in inches/cm." };
---
<Layout title="PDF Resolution & Dimensions Calculator" seo={seo}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 py-16 prose">
    <h1>PDF Resolution (DPI) & Dimensions Calculator</h1>
    <p>Understanding the relationship between pixels, inches, and DPI (Dots Per Inch) is essential when preparing PDFs for print or optimizing them for web viewing.</p>

    <div class="not-prose bg-bg-surface border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 my-8 shadow-sm">
      <form id="calc-form" class="space-y-4">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <label for="width" class="block text-sm font-medium text-text-primary">Width (Pixels)</label>
            <input type="number" id="width" name="width" value="2480" min="1" class="mt-1 block w-full rounded border-gray-300 shadow-sm focus:border-brand-accent focus:ring-brand-accent" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="height" class="block text-sm font-medium text-text-primary">Height (Pixels)</label>
            <input type="number" id="height" name="height" value="3508" min="1" class="mt-1 block w-full rounded border-gray-300 shadow-sm focus:border-brand-accent focus:ring-brand-accent" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="target-dpi" class="block text-sm font-medium text-text-primary">Target Resolution (DPI)</label>
          <select id="target-dpi" name="target-dpi" class="mt-1 block w-full rounded border-gray-300 shadow-sm focus:border-brand-accent focus:ring-brand-accent">
            <option value="72">72 (Web/Screen)</option>
            <option value="150">150 (Standard Print)</option>
            <option value="300" selected>300 (High-Res Print)</option>
            <option value="600">600 (Archival Print)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary w-full">Calculate Physical Dimensions</button>
      </form>

      <div id="result-container" class="mt-6 hidden p-4 bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-brand-accent rounded">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">Physical Dimensions:</h3>
        <p id="result-inches" class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-accent mt-2"></p>
        <p id="result-cm" class="text-text-secondary mt-1"></p>
        <p id="result-standard" class="text-sm font-medium mt-2"></p>
      </div>

      <noscript>
        <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 rounded">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">Manual Calculation Method</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">Since JavaScript is disabled, use this formula: <br/>
          <code>Inches = Pixels / DPI</code> <br/>
          <code>Centimeters = (Pixels / DPI) * 2.54</code></p>
        </div>
      </noscript>
    </div>

    <h2>How DPI Affects PDFs</h2>
    <p>A PDF inherently uses "points" for measurement (1 point = 1/72 of an inch). When you embed a raster image into a PDF, the DPI tells the viewer or printer how dense those pixels should be packed.</p>

    <h3>Common Standard Sizes (at 300 DPI)</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Standard Size</th>
          <th>Physical Dimensions</th>
          <th>Required Pixels (@300 DPI)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>A4 (International)</td>
          <td>8.27 x 11.69 inches (210 x 297 mm)</td>
          <td>2480 x 3508 px</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>US Letter</td>
          <td>8.5 x 11.0 inches</td>
          <td>2550 x 3300 px</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>If you find your file sizes are too large at 300 DPI, check out our <a href="/calculators/calc-1">File Size Estimator</a> or consider switching to 150 DPI. For more on PDF structure, see <a href="/reference/topic-1">PDF Specifications</a>.</p>

    <div class="mt-12 not-prose p-6 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Request a custom tool</h3>
      <CaptureForm formLabel="contact" submitText="Send Request" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById('calc-form');
  const resultContainer = document.getElementById('result-container');
  const resultInches = document.getElementById('result-inches');
  const resultCm = document.getElementById('result-cm');
  const resultStandard = document.getElementById('result-standard');

  if (form && resultContainer && resultInches && resultCm && resultStandard) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      const formData = new FormData(e.target as HTMLFormElement);
      const width = Number(formData.get('width'));
      const height = Number(formData.get('height'));
      const dpi = Number(formData.get('target-dpi'));

      const widthInches = width / dpi;
      const heightInches = height / dpi;

      const widthCm = widthInches * 2.54;
      const heightCm = heightInches * 2.54;

      resultInches.textContent = `${widthInches.toFixed(2)}″ × ${heightInches.toFixed(2)}″`;
      resultCm.textContent = `${widthCm.toFixed(1)} cm × ${heightCm.toFixed(1)} cm`;

      // Heuristic for matching standard sizes
      let standardMatch = "";
      if (Math.abs(widthInches - 8.27) < 0.1 && Math.abs(heightInches - 11.69) < 0.1) {
        standardMatch = "Matches A4 Paper Size.";
      } else if (Math.abs(widthInches - 8.5) < 0.1 && Math.abs(heightInches - 11.0) < 0.1) {
        standardMatch = "Matches US Letter Size.";
      } else {
        standardMatch = "Custom Size.";
      }

      resultStandard.textContent = standardMatch;
      resultContainer.classList.remove('hidden');
    });
  }
</script>
